rsz: trace every endpoint visit of the setup sweep, for the repair-yield study

Study instrumentation from the repair-knobs campaign
(ideas/repair-knobs-nihl.md, Phase 0 of the yield study). Not upstreamed;
carried while the campaign runs. It changes no result: every query it
adds is one the next pass would have made anyway or is read-only.

One [RSZ-ENDPOINTS] line per phase start with twenty-one quantiles of the
violating endpoint slacks, and one [RSZ-ENDPOINT] line per endpoint
visited by the LEGACY or LAST_GASP sweep: its index in the sweep, the
pass it started at, the passes and seconds it took, the endpoint slack,
the WNS and the TNS before and after, the pass of its first and last
improvement, the depth of its worst path, candidates, attempts and
accepted moves, the net moves committed by type, every improving pass with
the TNS it bought, the analytical size-up estimate and load delay of the
path at entry, and why the visit
ended (closed, no_change, stuck, terminate, rejected, over_area,
max_iter, max_passes).

The question it answers: which endpoints pay, in what order the sweep
reaches them, and what they cost -- whether a yield-ordered sweep is
possible and which endpoints defeat a stopping rule. The wall of an arm
carrying this patch is not to be read; each visit adds a TNS query.

